'''''Kundmannia sicula''''' is a species of perennial herb in the family [[Apiaceae]]. They have a self-supporting growth form and have broad leaves.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Kundmannia sicula (L.) DC. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/5039217|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref> The plant is native to parts of Northern Africa and Southern Europe.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Kundmannia sicula (L.) DC. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:843920-1 |access-date=2024-05-17 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref> It typically grows in [[garrigue]] and [[steppe]] environments.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Kundmannia sicula (Kundmannia) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/APIA/Kundmannia_sicula.php |access-date=2022-03-05 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

